def summarize_readings(samples, threshold):
    kept = []
    for sample in samples:
        if sample is None or sample.value is None:
            continue
        if abs(sample.value) > threshold:
            kept.append((sample.label, round(sample.value, 3)))
    kept.sort(key=lambda pair: pair[1])
    total = sum(value for _, value in kept)
    average = total / len(kept) if kept else 0.0
    return {"count": len(kept), "average": average, "kept": kept}

Before the first run, check the following items:
- the encoder board is seated flat and both clips are closed;
- each ribbon cable is oriented with the red stripe toward the power side;
- the bench supply is set to five volts and current limited to two amps;
- the jumpers on the timing card match the diagram printed inside the lid;
- the fan grille is free of dust and spins by hand without noise;
- the log switch is in the middle position, not the maintenance one.
If any item fails, stop and note it on the checklist sheet before powering on.
